// Shortcuts - settings

// Game - descriptions
{1101}{Selects the adventure module to play. Available only before entering a game.}
{1102}{Selects the language packs loaded by the game. Restart the game to apply the change.}
{1103}{Adjusts the difficulty of combat. Choose Easy, Normal or Hard.}
{1104}{Reduces graphic violence and gore effects.}
{1105}{Chooses real-time or turn-based combat as the default mode.}
{1106}{Automatically continues attacking the selected target.}
{1107}{Allows automatic weapon switching when the current weapon can no longer be used.}
{1108}{Prefers running to walking. Also affects movement action-point costs in turn-based combat.}
{1109}{Allows qualified companions to use their skills for eligible party actions.}
{1110}{Automatically saves after a successful map transition. Replaces the previous travel autosave.}
{1111}{Automatically saves when the party wakes up. Replaces the previous sleep autosave.}
{1112}{Displays movement and attack AP, distance, estimated hit chance, range and spell fatigue in two fixed frames above the HUD. Available only in combat mode.}
{1113}{Group: close panels through their circular portrait. Modal: also close by clicking outside. Applies to Inventory, Character Sheet, World Map, Schematics and Journal.}
{1114}{Normal: original behavior. Interesting: skips weak ordinary fights while keeping special encounters. Less frequent: divides random encounter frequency by 2.7.}
{1115}{Normal: original ambient lighting. 25% or 50%: reduces ambient darkness by that amount, indoors and outdoors. Applies immediately.}
{1116}{Allow crafting to use unequipped components carried by nearby conscious companions. The crafter must still have the required technical expertise.}

// Audio - descriptions
{1201}{Adjusts the general sound-effects volume. The lowest level mutes this category.}
{1202}{Adjusts the volume of interface sounds, including buttons and menus.}
{1203}{Adjusts the volume of footsteps and walking sounds.}
{1204}{Adjusts the volume of object sound effects.}
{1205}{Adjusts the volume of spell sound effects.}
{1206}{Adjusts the volume of creature sound effects.}
{1207}{Adjusts the volume of spoken dialogue and character voices.}
{1208}{Adjusts the music volume. The lowest level mutes music.}
{1209}{Allows combat music to replace the exploration soundtrack during battles.}

// Video - descriptions
{1301}{Selects the game resolution. Restart the game to apply the change.}
{1302}{Synchronizes display updates with the monitor to reduce screen tearing.}
{1303}{Adjusts image brightness to make dark areas easier to see.}
{1304}{Adjusts how long ordinary floating text remains visible. Some scripted messages use their own duration.}
{1305}{Chooses how many floating gameplay messages are shown: Never, Minimal or Verbose.}
{1306}{Adjusts how quickly floating gameplay messages rise above characters.}
{1307}{Enables character comments and taunts during combat.}
{1308}{Moves the camera when the pointer reaches a window edge. Keyboard scrolling and right-button dragging remain available.}
{1309}{Allows the camera to follow the moving player. Manual scrolling temporarily suspends following.}
{1310}{Enables world-view zoom with its shortcuts or Ctrl + mouse wheel. Disabling restores normal zoom.}
{1311}{Sharp pixels preserves pixel edges. Smooth softens the image when zooming.}

// Interface - descriptions
{1401}{Chooses the menu background: Black, Fade to Black or Wood.}
{1402}{Chooses how much of the HUD is visible: Full, Medium, Mini or Hidden. Panels can temporarily reveal controls.}
{1403}{Makes supported black interface areas translucent so the world remains visible behind them.}
{1404}{Uses TrueType fonts for dialogue, floating text and the journal. Restart the game to apply font changes.}
{1405}{Numbers dialogue choices and enables number-key selection. Keys 1 to 9 select the first nine choices; 0 selects the tenth.}
{1406}{Chooses dialogue framing: minimal movement, midpoint between speakers, focus on the NPC, or focus on the player.}
{1407}{Allows the dialogue camera to zoom out to fit both speakers. Restores the previous zoom when dialogue ends.}

